From 301d5ddf5bdccb434d207a1930d83b9335378aee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Majid Arasskhani <M.Arasskhani@gosilkroad.net>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 14:06:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/10] feat(ops): /ready probe, app healthcheck/restart,
 graceful shutdown for streams

The alpha-router container had no healthcheck and no restart policy, /health
was a constant, and uvicorn was stopped with Docker's default 10s grace while
proxy_read_timeout lets chat streams run for an hour -- every deploy killed
in-flight (already reserved) turns and a dead worker stayed dead.

- app/services/readiness_service.py + GET /ready: database and redis are
  required (503 when either fails); qdrant and object storage are reported as
  degraded but never fail the probe, so a Qdrant outage does not restart-loop
  chat. Every check has a 2s timeout; details never include connection
  strings. /health stays the deliberately constant liveness answer.
- docker-compose.yml: alpha-router gets restart: unless-stopped,
  stop_grace_period: 120s, a /ready healthcheck (15s interval, 90s
  start_period) and 'uvicorn --timeout-graceful-shutdown 110' so in-flight
  streams can finish and settle before SIGKILL. postgres, pgbouncer, redis and
  seaweedfs gain restart: unless-stopped (only clamav/qdrant had one). The
  edge now waits for alpha-router to be healthy instead of merely started.

Tests: tests/test_readiness.py (required vs degraded, timeout bound,
endpoint status codes).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UTnpHajSmkk2JMLfuQoV7o
